From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:44:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] tcp_timer: drop a peer that stops answering window probes

The persist timer probed a closed window forever. A peer that is still
there answers every probe, even while its window stays closed, but one
that vanished never does, so its connection, and for a host-forwarded
or NAT connection the host socket, stayed open for as long as libslirp
ran. Retransmission gives up on a silent peer; persistence did not.

Drop the connection once the peer has been silent for TCP_MAXIDLE, the
time keep-alive waits on unanswered probes (10 minutes). Probes go out
at most 60 seconds apart, so a live peer resets the idle time long
before that.
---
 src/tcp_timer.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/tcp_timer.c b/src/tcp_timer.c
index 1d4bcc1919cacc687f626b07d6db2c257328186e..d4b5739af268c1259c14a5f090ed9afca9bd5711 100644
--- a/src/tcp_timer.c
+++ b/src/tcp_timer.c
@@ -238,6 +238,17 @@ static struct tcpcb *tcp_timers(register struct tcpcb *tp, int timer)
      * Force a byte to be output, if possible.
      */
     case TCPT_PERSIST:
+        /*
+         * A peer that is still there answers every window probe, even while
+         * its window stays closed. One that has been silent for as long as
+         * keep-alive waits on unanswered probes is gone: drop the connection
+         * rather than probe it for as long as libslirp runs, holding the
+         * host socket open.
+         */
+        if (tp->t_idle >= TCP_MAXIDLE) {
+            tp = tcp_drop(tp, 0);
+            break;
+        }
         tcp_setpersist(tp);
         tp->t_force = 1;
         tcp_output(tp);
